  "entries": [
    {
      "logbook": {
        "entryId": "M.LOG-0001",
        "timestamp": "2074-08-16T14:30:00.000Z",
        "type": "mission_log",
        "tags": ["OERA", "dry_dock", "mission", "tasks"],
        "author": {
          "company": "O.E.R.A - Oceanic Exploration and Research Alliance.",
          "department": "Operations Command",
          "name": "Admiral Catherine Okafor",
          "role": "Director of Operations"
        },
        "content": "{captain},\n\nCongratulations on your new command of the world's most advanced submarine ever built. The Aqua Nova Deep Sea Research Vessel (DSV) represents mankind's desire for exploration and discovery, not of distant stars, but of the depths of our oceans at our feet. Your mission is to seek out new life where no light has ever reached. To explore, rescue, and protect. You are to become the guardian of the ocean, for beneath the waves lies our future.\n\nYour first task is to commission the Aqua Nova with a series of system tests. I apologise for the haste, but she must be out of dry dock and underway. Your trials orders will follow once you are aboard. Until she is commissioned, do not exceed 15 knots or 300 meters.\n\nThere will be friendly vessels in the area while testing is being conducted. You may be the most formidable ship out there, but not everyone wants to see you succeed. The Aqua Nova is still untested and your crew still new.\n\nWhen the time comes, you are to push the limits of speed and figure out where they are. Computer models and theory can only take us so far. The Aqua Nova has a state-of-the-art hull skin, designed for high-speed supercavitation, paired with a new hydro-jet propulsion system and a quantum fusion drive to power you. You should be able to get over 100 knots.\n\nThis is your digital logbook. Mission orders, results and discoveries are recorded here, and each mission entry is also a save point you can return to. Please keep it up to date.\n\nYour PED is on your bed and your communicator pin is on your desk. Collect both. Put the pin on and call ARIA, your Executive Officer. She will take it from there.\n\nWith confidence,\nAdmiral Catherine Okafor\nDirector of Operations, O.E.R.A.",
        "tasks": [
          "Collect your PED from the bed",
          "Collect your communicator pin from the desk",
          "Call ARIA, your Executive Officer",
          "Find your way to the Bridge"
        ],
        "completedTasks": []
      },
